course: dictionary
lesson: 10099
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. These words are its context, and they leave clues. «Your thigh is the top part of your leg, between your hip and your knee.» Here thigh is a part of your body.
explain: The same word can mean something different in another sentence. «Roast chicken thighs were on the menu.» Now a thigh is a piece of chicken that you eat. The clue is the word chicken, because you cannot eat your own leg.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits. In «The big thigh muscles push the pedals down», the word pedals tells you the thigh is part of a body doing a job, like cycling. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Some words join together to make a new meaning. «Thigh bone» is the bone in the top part of your leg. «Thigh-high» describes something that reaches up to your thigh, like a sock or a boot.
fact: The thigh is the top part of your leg, between your hip and your knee.
fact: A thigh is also the top part of a chicken leg, which people eat as food.
fact: «The femur, or thigh bone, is the longest and strongest bone in the body.»
fact: Thigh muscles help you run, jump and push the pedals on a bike.
fact: «A dead leg» happens when a thigh muscle is squashed against the bone; it needs rest and cold, not hard rubbing.
exercise: «Roast chicken thighs were on the menu.» What does thigh mean here? | *A piece of chicken eaten as food | The top part of your leg | A bone in your arm | A kind of sock
exercise: «The femur, or thigh bone, is the longest and strongest bone in the body.» Which bone is this? | The thumb | The kneecap | *The femur | The shoulder blade
exercise: «The big thigh muscles push the pedals down.» Which word is the clue that thigh means part of the body doing a job? | *pedals | down | big | muscles
test: Kian says «Ma leg's deid!» What does deid mean? | Warm | *Dead | Broken | Very long
test: «Thigh muscles help you run and jump.» What do thigh muscles do? | Store food | Keep you warm | Grow hair | *Help you run and jump
exam: Which meaning of thigh fits «The chicken thigh was crispy and golden»? | A way of standing still | A bone in your face | *A piece of chicken eaten as food | The top part of your leg
